{"availability":"available","full":"SpringTimeCode/SpiroJS","name":"SpiroJS","description":"Animated spiral circle graphs in the browser — a port of a 1982 Commodore 64 BASIC program.","category":"Design","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-11-29T22:31:41Z","updated":"2026-10-10T22:00:32Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://springtimecode.github.io/SpiroJS/","topics":["bootstrap","canvas","commodore-64","creative-coding","fontawesome","generative-art","javascript","pwa","spirograph"],"demo":"https://springtimecode.github.io/SpiroJS/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:56.995Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:56.995Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T21:13:56.995Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.149Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T21:13:56.995Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SpiroJS draws animated spiral circle graphs using sine and cosine trigonometry functions. It uses JavaScript, Font Awesome, and Bootstrap 5.","This is code converted from my original 1982 Commodore 64 Basic program."],"features":["Animated plots: play forward or backward and watch the pattern evolve as the loop multiplier changes.","Presets and random settings: start from a curated preset or shuffle the settings to discover new patterns.","Undo, redo and reset: step back through changes, or return everything to the defaults.","Precise control: type an exact value into any setting, or fine-tune the loop multiplier by scrolling or dragging sideways on the canvas.","Color modes: Mono, Rainbow, Sunset, and Ocean gradients along the curve, with an optional glow."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SpringTimeCode/SpiroJS/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"de57a188ac00dd4cfe4bc2c12fba8942f6f2c2867b9556635f2f10ec5eeb68eb","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.290Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:10.290Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text"